Subject: [PATCH] 4657: a company word in the owner's own label becomes
 likely_employer (switch OFF)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The prompt chat's test 1 (box 54353): a contact saved „<name> Arci" — asked
where she works, the run said the workplace is not in the record, 2 of 3.

The contact profile now carries likely_employer: a word or adjacent pair from
the owner's OWN saved name or tags for that number that at least two people
hold as their employer (member profiles and employer facts, Georgian capitals
folded). Only the owner's own words are read; the employers it is matched
against are a count. 39 ms on production for the founder's „Arci" case.

LIKELY_EMPLOYER_NOTE is model-facing (D44): the switch stays false until
Misho's yes on its exact text; until then the profile is unchanged.

